# Coach speech (Estonian): the building blocks every line uses (src/coach/catalog.cpp renders them).
# Same keys as assets/coach/speech/en/common.lang, plus the grammatical forms Estonian needs.
# Register: the coach says "sina" to the player ("sa", "sinu", imperatives in the singular); the game
# menus stay formal ("te"). Estonian has no grammatical gender: nothing agrees with the sex of the coach
# or of the player, and a pronoun standing for a piece is the same for every piece. See the glossary
# (glossary/et.md of the translation brief) for the chess terms.

# ---- Pieces --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nouns: ettur, ratsu, oda, vanker, lipp, kuningas (no gender). The possessives "sinu" / "minu" do not
# inflect, so the case lives on the noun only; the colours "valge" / "must" (Analysis mode) agree in
# case with the noun, except in the terminative, essive, abessive and comitative, where an attribute
# stays in the genitive ("valge ratsuga", not "valgega ratsuga").
#
# Every form below is defined for all six pieces and all four owners (your, my, white, black). Three
# series of the 14 cases:
#   <case>       with the possessive: sinu / minu ratsu (your, my), valge / must ratsu (white, black)
#   own_<case>   with the reflexive "oma": Estonian says "oma", not "sinu" / "minu", whenever the owner
#                is the subject of the clause, also the implied subject of an imperative or of an
#                infinitive: "Kaitse oma kuningat!", "Ma toon oma vankri mängu.", "Valge kaotab oma
#                lipu." Use "sinu" / "minu" only when someone else is the subject: "Minu oda ründab
#                sinu vankrit."
#   bare_<case>  the noun alone, no possessive: for a statement about the kind of piece, or where the
#                owner is plain ("Ratsu käib L-tähe kujuliselt.", "Käi ratsuga.")
# Objects: a total object is in the genitive in a statement ("Ma löön {your:gen}." = "sinu vankri"),
# in the nominative in an imperative, a passive or after "tuleb / peab + da" ("Löö {my}!" = "minu
# vanker"); a partial object is in the partitive: unfinished actions, verbs of attacking, defending,
# threatening, moving, looking ("ründab {your:part}"), and every object of a negative verb.
# Pronouns: no form is needed: "see" (it) is the same for every piece; write it directly (see, selle,
# seda, sellesse, selles, sellest, sellele, sellel, sellelt, selleks, selleni, sellena, selleta,
# sellega), or "ta / tema" where the piece acts ("Vanker on tugev. Ta liigub sirgjooneliselt.").
# Never attach an ending to a placeholder: "{your}ga" is wrong, "{your:com}" is right.
#
# Form         your (my, white, black)      example
#   nom        sinu ratsu (valge ratsu)     "{your} on ohus." / imperative object "Löö {my}!"
#   gen        sinu vankri (valge vankri)   "Ma löön {your:gen}.", "{my:gen} ees", "{your:gen} kõrval"
#   part       sinu vankrit (valget vankrit) "Ma ründan {your:part}.", "Ära jäta {my:part} tähelepanuta."
#   ill        sinu lipusse (valgesse lipusse) "See ähvardus puutub {my:ill}." (into; rare)
#   ine        sinu lipus (valges lipus)    "Kogu jõud on {your:ine}." (in)
#   ela        sinu odast (valgest odast)   "Räägime {my:ela}.", "{your:ela} sõltub kõik." (from, about)
#   all        sinu kuningale (valgele kuningale) "Ma annan {your:all} tuld.", "Ma lähenen {your:all}." (to, onto)
#   ade        sinu ratsul (valgel ratsul)  "{your:ade} pole kaitset." (on; X has)
#   abl        sinu vankrilt (valgelt vankrilt) "Ma võtan {your:abl} kaitse ära." (off, from)
#   tra        sinu lipuks (valgeks lipuks) "See ettur muundub peagi {my:tra}." (into, as a result)
#   ter        sinu kuningani (valge kuningani) "Minu vanker jõuab {your:ter}." (as far as)
#   ess        sinu lipuna (valge lipuna)   "Ettur jätkab mängu {your:ess}." (as)
#   abe        sinu liputa (valge liputa)   "{your:abe} oleks sul raske." (without)
#   com        sinu ratsuga (valge ratsuga) "Minu oda vahetub {your:com}." (with)
#   own_nom    oma vanker                   "Too {your:own_nom} mängu!" (imperative total object)
#   own_gen    oma vankri                   "Sa jätsid {your:own_gen} kaitseta.", "Ma toon {my:own_gen} mängu."
#   own_part   oma kuningat                 "Kaitse {your:own_part}!", "Ma liigutan {my:own_part}."
#   own_ill    oma lipusse                  "Ära kiindu {your:own_ill}."
#   own_ine    oma vankris                  "Kas oled {your:own_ine} kindel?"
#   own_ela    oma odast                    "Sa loobusid {your:own_ela}."
#   own_all    oma kuningale                "Mõtle {your:own_all}!"
#   own_ade    oma ratsul                   "Lase {your:own_ade} töötada."
#   own_abl    oma ratsult                  "Sa võtsid {your:own_abl} kaitse ära."
#   own_tra    oma lipuks                   "Sa võid selle etturi teha {your:own_tra}."
#   own_ter    oma etturini                 "Vii kuningas {your:own_ter}."
#   own_ess    oma lipuna                   "Sa saad etturi tagasi {your:own_ess}."
#   own_abe    oma liputa                   "Sa jäid {your:own_abe}."
#   own_com    oma ratsuga                  "Löö {your:own_com}!", "Ma lõin {my:own_com}."
#   bare_nom   ratsu                        "{your:bare_nom} käib L-tähe kujuliselt."
#   bare_gen   ratsu                        "See on tüüpiline {your:bare_gen} käik."
#   bare_part  ratsut                       "Liiguta {your:bare_part}."
#   bare_ill   kuningasse                   "Kõik puutub {your:bare_ill}."
#   bare_ine   ratsus                       "{your:bare_ine} on peidus suur jõud."
#   bare_ela   ratsust                      "Alusta {your:bare_ela}."
#   bare_all   ratsule                      "Anna {your:bare_all} vaba väli."
#   bare_ade   ratsul                       "{your:bare_ade} on kaheksa võimalikku käiku."
#   bare_abl   vankrilt                     "Mine {my:bare_abl} eemale."
#   bare_tra   lipuks                       "Ettur muundub {your:bare_tra}."
#   bare_ter   kuningani                    "Sa jõuad {my:bare_ter}."
#   bare_ess   lipuna                       "Ettur jätkab {your:bare_ess}."
#   bare_abe   liputa                       "{your:bare_abe} on raske kaitsta."
#   bare_com   ratsuga                      "Käi {your:bare_com}."
# The same forms exist for {t1} {t2} {your2} {my2}, and for {piece} {t1} {t2} of the Analysis mode
# (owner white / black: "valge ratsu", "musta vankrit", "valgele lipule"; own_ = "oma", bare_ = noun).
